# Advisory only, and deliberately so.
#
# The authoritative run of this check is the Branch Policy workflow: it sees the full graph, the
# pushed tag, and every published ref. This hook exists for one thing -- naming an off-policy branch
# while renaming it is still one command -- so it must never block a push, and `--offline` keeps it
# off the network: a fetch in a push path turns a slow remote into one that looks hung. `|| true`
# because a local clone can legitimately be stale (a `stage` never fetched, a tag that is not here),
# and a push is not the place to resolve that.
node scripts/check-branch-policy.mjs --offline || true
